 ],
 "storyArc": "Vale and Hernando are horrified by everything Tomás has never done: never tried ajiaco, never played tejo, never climbed Monserrate. He has not read the café's lease yet either. Then a man in a beautiful suit orders a cappuccino, tips too much, and asks Tomás: \"¿Ha pensado en vender?\". His name is Ricardo Altamira. The month ends: they have taken $2.130.000. Tomás has lost the bet, and he is oddly happy about it."
